## When to Get Your Christmas Nails Done (So They Last)

<strong>When should you get your nails done for christmas so they last?</strong> Book roughly two to three weeks before Christmas Day for a fresh set that carries cleanly through New Year's Eve. Gel polish holds for two to three weeks with proper application, which means a set done too early risks looking tired by December 31st, while a set done too late might mean rebooking mid-holiday season when appointments are hardest to get.

This is the piece almost no other <strong>christmas nails</strong> guide addresses, and it's one of the most searched practical questions around the topic for a reason. A gel manicure applied in the first week of December generally holds its shine and shape through both Christmas and New Year's, provided the base application was clean and the tips are sealed properly. Regular polish, by comparison, tends to show wear within five to seven days, which makes it a better fit for a single-event look than a two-holiday stretch.

If your plan includes touch-ups or a color change between Christmas and New Year's, booking your initial appointment slightly earlier and scheduling a quick refresh in the days before NYE solves the timing gap entirely. Either way, the appointment itself matters less than the plan around it, and knowing the two-to-three-week window in advance means one less thing to figure out during an already busy month.

