## Pick Your Lane, Not Every Option

A hundred and twenty ideas were never meant to all apply to you at once. The point of grouping <strong>christmas nails</strong> by color, then motif, then formality was to get you to three or four options you'd actually book, not a mental list you'll forget by tomorrow. That's the difference between a mood board and a decision.

Save the color that caught your eye first. Pair it with the motif that fits your actual week, an accent wreath for a party, a plain gold tip for the office, a full character set for a day you don't have anywhere to be. Then book two to three weeks out and let the rest sort itself. Nothing about a good manicure requires covering every base at once. It requires picking the right one and committing to it.

